<title>ITALY: Reuters Asset Allocation Poll (Italy) - March.</title>
<headline>Reuters Asset Allocation Poll (Italy) - March.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian funds and banks are more cautious over domestic financial markets and have increased their weight on cash and also slightly on foreign markets, a Reuters Asset Allocation Poll for March showed on Friday.</p>
<p>Reuters collected the banks' and funds' allocation from Monday to Wednesday February 26. The survey shows that in the Italian bond market, the short term and medium term sectors have been neglected in favour of floating rate certficates (CCTs) and of long term paper. Analysts noted that CCTs were also attractive because of their safe-haven status in the currently uncertain Italian economic and political environment.</p>
<p>Centrosim has revised its benchmark for its international portfolio, reducing its total weight on Italy.</p>
<p>Some of the averages have been distorted by the fact that not all contributors have a comparison with the previous month and therefore the number of participants is different.</p>
